{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>He took my birthright, etc.</b> Why did he say that he took the birthright through deception and guile, when he sold it to him of his own free will? And if Esau despised the birthright, what is Jacob's fault in this? And what seems closest to me to say on this is that Esau said one thing depends on the other — for when Isaac asked him, ״מִי אַתָּה״ (Genesis 27:18), and he answered him, ״אָנֹכִי עֵשָׂו בְּכֹרֶךָ״ (Genesis 27:19), and how could he utter a falsehood from his mouth — is it not so that ״שְׁאֵרִית יִשְׂרָאֵל לֹא יְדַבְּרוּ כָזָב״ (Zephaniah 3:13)? Rather, he surely said to him, 'I am in the place of Esau your firstborn,' for I acquired the birthright from him, and if so I am in his place. And had he not acquired the birthright he could not have answered, 'I am Esau your firstborn,' nor could he have come to receive the blessings at all. And surely at the time he acquired the birthright his intention was to deceive me through this, for he would call himself such. And the reason he accuses him regarding the taking of the birthright is because he says: now the matter has become known, for the purchase is a mistaken sale. For at first I thought that there is no superiority to the birthright beyond taking a double portion after my father's death, and I thought that perhaps my father would not leave anything behind, therefore I sold it for a trifle. But now I see that the birthright is worth a great deal, for the blessings depend on it — for why did Jacob say, ״אָנֹכִי עֵשָׂו בְּכֹרֶךָ״? Why did he need to mention the birthright? Rather, surely it is because by virtue of the birthright he is worthy of ״יֶתֶר שְׂאֵת וְיֶתֶר עָז״ (Genesis 49:3), and through this ״יַעְקְבֵנִי״ (Genesis 27:36) — for I did not know that receiving the blessings depends on the birthright. A hint to the matter: בְּכֹר ('firstborn') has the same letters as בֵּרֵךְ ('bless'). Therefore he said, ״וַיַּעְקְבֵנִי זֶה פַעֲמַיִם״ (Genesis 27:36) — but the act of harming is only one."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:37.745382411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}